<SocialAgentPage
  current="overview"
  title="Social Agent"
  lead="A privately operated tool for curating, publishing, and reviewing the performance of Shariq Hirani's content."
  description="Information about Social Agent, a private content publishing and growth-reporting tool operated by Shariq Hirani."
>
  <p>
    Social Agent supports publishing for this engineering site and Oris. It is
    operated privately by Shariq Hirani rather than offered as a public
    dashboard, signup product, or multi-user service.
  </p>

  <h2>What it does</h2>

  <p>
    Notion remains the place where content is curated and approved. Social Agent
    can prepare channel-specific drafts, publish approved work when its
    scheduled time arrives, and record the result. Publication still requires
    both a human <strong>Approved</strong> decision and a due
    <strong>Post at</strong> time.
  </p>

  <p>
    An optional growth-reporting subsystem reads content inventory and provider
    metrics, keeps source-labelled observations, and creates deterministic
    private reports. Those reports help the operator decide what to improve.
    Analytics cannot grant approval, change the publishing schedule, or publish
    content.
  </p>

  <h2>Google access</h2>

  <p>
    When the owner connects a Google account, Social Agent requests only
    read-only access needed for Search Console and YouTube reporting. It reads
    search performance for authorized properties and metadata plus aggregate
    viewing and engagement statistics for the authorized YouTube channel. It
    does not receive a Google password, upload videos, or delete videos through
    these permissions.
  </p>

  <h2>Information for authorized users</h2>

  <p>
    Access to the tool is limited to the operator and people the operator
    explicitly authorizes. Review the <a href="/social-agent/privacy/"
      >privacy notice</a
    > for details about Google data and storage, and the
    <a href="/social-agent/terms/">terms and use information</a> for the boundaries
    of this private tool.
  </p>
</SocialAgentPage>
